antity.value`, and `valueCodeableConcept.coding`. Changes to those fields would change the observations fed into the historical data source.\n\n**Likely but not a real dependency**\n\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-form-entry-app/src/openmrs-esm-framework.mock.ts:41` declares its own `FHIRResource` interface. It would not follow a real framework change, and it could hide one in tests.\n\n**Not checked**\n\n- Callers of the form-data-source function at `form-data-source.service.ts:227`, and the consumers of `useVitalsAndBiometrics`, were not traced. The consumers use `MappedVitals`, not `FHIRResource`, so they are only indirectly affected.\n- Other `openmrs-esm-core` consumers of `FHIRResource` were out of scope for this question. A Falkon reference lookup in core returned only the definition and a docs page, `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/interfaces/FHIRResource.md:1-3`.\n- The Falkon search budget was partly used by failed calls under the wrong repository name, so the grep coverage of the chart is the local checkout plus one Falkon lookup.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-emr-api/src/types/fhir-resource.ts\", \"startLine\": 1, \"endLine\": 26},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-vitals-app/src/common/types.ts\", \"startLine\": 1, \"endLine\": 8},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-vitals-app/src/common/data.resource.ts\", \"startLine\": 561, \"endLine\": 566},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-vitals-app/src/common/data.resource.ts\", \"startLine\": 2, \"endLine\": 10},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-form-entry-app/src/app/form-data-source/form-data-source.service.ts\", \"startLine\": 227, \"endLine\": 264},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-form-entry-app/src/app/form-data-source/form-data-source.service.ts\", \"startLine\": 6, \"endLine\": 6},\n  {\"path\": \"open